  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Strengthening Societal and Economic Resilience in Jordan (SSERJ)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The programme will expand contributory social insurance schemes which will allow more informal jobs to be formalised. It will also support an expansion of tax-financed social assistance schemes, seeking greater coherence between national systems and those supporting refugees to improve efficiency.  Frontloaded financial support will demonstrate proof of concept which, alongside technical support, is appropriate assistance to a Low Middle Income Country. A comprehensive sustainability strategy and exit plan for UK support will be developed during the inception period and monitored throughout implementation of this programme.</narrative>
  </description>
